<section class="section surface">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <span class="kicker">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="h1" style="margin: 20px 0 16px;">Cookie policy.</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: <%= Date.today.strftime('%B %Y') %></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm surface-alt rule-top rule-bottom">
  <div class="wrap-narrow legal-prose">

    <h2 class="h2">1. What cookies are</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small data files placed on your device when you visit a website. They let a site remember your session, understand how the site is used and(in some cases) personalise content.</p>

    <h2 class="h2">2. Consilix&rsquo;s cookie use</h2>
    <p>consilix.ai is deliberately minimal. We use:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> required for the site to function &mdash; e.g. CSRF protection on the contact form.</li>
      <li><strong>No advertising cookies.</strong> We do not run ad-tech.</li>
      <li><strong>No cross-site tracking.</strong> We do not embed retargeting pixels.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>If we ever add privacy-respecting analytics (e.g. Plausible, Fathom), we&rsquo;ll note it here.</p>

    <h2 class="h2">3. Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can block or delete cookies via your browser settings. Blocking essential cookies may prevent the contact form from working.</p>

    <h2 class="h2">4. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions: <a class="link-text" href="mailto:hello@consilix.ai">hello@consilix.ai</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 { margin: 40px 0 14px; }
  .legal-prose h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal-prose p { max-width: 64ch; margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .legal-prose ul { margin: 0 0 16px 1.2em; padding: 0; }
  .legal-prose li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-2); margin-bottom: 8px; max-width: 64ch; }
  .legal-prose strong { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
